Makes regular washing noticeably easier
Ceramic Coating Myths Debunked: Does It Stop Scratches?
One of the most persistent ceramic coating myths is that it makes your car completely immune to scratches. In reality, it adds a layer of hardness that helps with light swirl marks, but it won't stop deeper scratches from keys or branches.
Reduces the chance of fine swirl marks from washing
Does not prevent deep scratches from sharp contact
Careful washing habits are still worth keeping up
Ceramic Coating Myths Debunked: The Self-Cleaning Car Idea
Another common myth is that a coated car basically cleans itself. Ceramic coating makes dirt slide off more easily, but it doesn't stop your car from getting dirty in the first place.
Regular washing keeps the coating performing at its best
Dirt and dust still land on the surface, just easier to rinse away
Skipping washes for too long can still lead to buildup
Ceramic Coating Myths Debunked: One and Done, Forever
