Frequently Asked Questions
What does ceramic coating genuinely shield a car from? UV rays, oxidation, and mild chemical stains, and it also makes dirt easier to rinse off during a wash.
Is regular maintenance still part of owning a coated car? Yes, the car still needs routine washing and light upkeep to keep the coating working the way it should.
How long can ceramic coating be expected to last? About 1 to 2 years for consumer-grade products, with professional-grade versions often reaching 3 to 5 years or more.
Is it true that ceramic coating makes a car scratch-proof? Not quite ; paint can still pick up deep scratches or other damage even after coating.
What are the downsides worth knowing before committing? A bigger upfront cost, the requirement for proper paint prep beforehand, and continued need for regular washing.
